{"type":"message","id":"08043ddc","parentId":"969b9d4e","timestamp":"2026-06-17T06:44:00.682Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"There is **no immediate concern** with HTTP/HTTPS here for two key reasons:\n\n### 1. TLS/HTTPS is Enforced (Your Credentials are Secure)\nAll communications with the site (`https://coinography.com`) are conducted over **HTTPS** (encrypted TLS). \n* **Why this matters:** The WordPress API uses Basic Authentication to transmit the Application Password. Because we are strictly using HTTPS, this credential is fully encrypted in transit. \n* If any part of the pipeline fell back to unencrypted **HTTP**, the Application Password would be transmitted in plaintext and could be easily intercepted. Fortunately, the server forces HTTPS, and our scripts are configured to use it.\n\n### 2. Protocol Version (HTTP/1.1 vs. HTTP/2)\nThe SiteGround WAF handles both HTTP/1.1 (used by Python `requests`) and HTTP/2 (used by `curl`) without issue. \n* The only critical detail was that the **User-Agent** header had to remain identical between the solver session and the publishing session. As long as they match, SiteGround’s Nginx firewall accepts the cookies regardless of whether the tool initiates an HTTP/1.1 or HTTP/2 connection."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gemini-3.5-flash","usage":{"input":93934,"output":723,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":94657,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1781678632309,"responseId":"K0Iyaqa-F4j8mLAPsIiZoQs"}}
