{"type":"message","id":"d8fcc349","parentId":"8b61c576","timestamp":"2026-06-17T06:47:03.285Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"In our context, we are using **HTTPS** (Secure). \n\nEvery single communication between Scribe and your WordPress website is strictly encrypted and secure.\n\nHere is exactly what we are using:\n\n1. **Target URLs:** Your configuration in `TOOLS.md` and the project settings specifically use `https://coinography.com`. Our scripts never make requests to unencrypted `http://` addresses.\n2. **Encryption in Transit:** Because we use `https://`, all your data—including your **WordPress Application Passwords**, article drafts, and images—is completely encrypted before it leaves this machine. \n3. **The Term \"HTTP\" in Logs:** When the terminal logs say things like `Image upload: HTTP 201` or `HTTP/2 200`, it is just using the standard names of the response messages. Those messages are wrapped in a secure SSL/TLS layer (hence, **HTTPS**).\n\nYou are **100% on HTTPS** and your credentials are completely safe."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gemini-3.5-flash","usage":{"input":6999,"output":767,"cacheRead":88007,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":95773,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1781678814989,"responseId":"4UIyavjiFuKw8uMPqKP7mAs"}}
